    "body": "## Summary\n- Add a Prebid best practices skill that audits GPID, consent modules, and floors through Chrome DevTools MCP.\n- Include a default prompt for invoking the skill.\n\n## Type of issue\nAgent tooling documentation.\n\n## Description\nThe skill guides an agent through Prebid's page-provided `summary` and `auctions` tools, then uses bidder network requests when outbound delivery needs confirmation. It reports observed auction state separately from configured state and limits consent-module judgments to applicable privacy regimes.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n1. Invoke `$prebid-best-practices` on a page with Prebid.js and Chrome DevTools MCP.\n2. Follow the skill's GPID, consent, and floor checks.\n3. Review the evidence and verdict table it produces.\n\n## Test page\nNot applicable; this PR adds an agent skill and no runtime code.\n\n### Expected results\nThe skill provides evidence-based GPID, consent-module, and floor findings, with clear limitations when a bidder payload or auction is unavailable.\n\n### Actual results\nThe skill and prompt files passed local structure and required-check validation. A live browser audit was not run because Chrome DevTools MCP was unavailable in the authoring session.\n\n## Platform details\nPrebid.js repository; Markdown and YAML only. No browser or Node.js version dependency added.\n\n## Other information\nThe skill builds on the existing `prebid-chrome-devtools` skill. No source or test files changed.\n\n## Validation\n- Local skill structure and required-check validation: passed.\n- `npx gulp lint`: not run (Markdown/YAML-only change).\n- `npx gulp test-only`: not run (Markdown/YAML-only change).",
